[366.276,"o","warning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one\r\n"]
[366.278,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[366.28,"o","   · read Terraform's plan of applying .openvidu/oracle again (nothing is changed)\r\n"]
[371.051,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your Oracle Cloud tenancy (region eu-madrid-1, compartment ***); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. Template: render the elastic template into .openvidu/oracle/tf-oracle-openvidu-pro-elastic.tf\r\n     and its variables into .openvidu/oracle/openvidu.auto.tfvars.json (0600)\r\n  2. Machines: they already exist, and it sets the media nodes to 2 (fixedNumberOfMediaNodes), and the ones it removes DRAIN first: each takes no new rooms and goes once the rooms, recordings and ingests on it end, and the apply waits for that (up to $OPENVIDU_MEDIA_DRAIN_TIMEOUT seconds, 7200 by default; past it the node goes as it is); `--mode assisted` prints the commands to read Terraform's plan first\r\n  3. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n\r\nWarning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud…\r\n   · initialize Terraform in .openvidu/oracle (downloads the provider)\r\n"]
[371.916,"o","   · apply .openvidu/oracle (this returns when Terraform is done)\r\n"]
[376.916,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so `ov stack destroy` removes it even if the wait below fails\r\n   ✓ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud\r\n\r\n▶ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu…\r\n"]
[378.366,"o","   · OpenVidu is up\r\n   ✓ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu\r\n\r\n▶ Register the stack…\r\n"]
[378.474,"o","\r\nStack described by the deployment:\r\n  name         openvidu-e2e-oci-el-s131730\r\n  deployment   elastic · oracle · pro\r\n  version      ov-admin\r\n  modules      dashboard, egress, ingress, meet, observability\r\n  dashboard    https://openvidu-oqaldo-141-253-198-88.sslip.io\r\n  published    by ov ov-admin on 2026-11-16 13:30 UTC (generation 1)\r\n\r\n"]
[378.477,"o","✔ registered stack \"openvidu-e2e-oci-el-s131730\" in <run>/openvidu-e2e-oci-el-s131730/stack\r\n   ✓ Register the stack\r\n\r\n✔ OpenVidu Pro (elastic) is up on Oracle Cloud\r\n  URL:          https://openvidu-oqaldo-141-253-198-88.sslip.io/\r\n  credentials:  oci secrets secret-bundle get-secret-bundle-by-name --secret-name OPENVIDU_URL --vault-id *** --query 'data.\"secret-bundle-content\".content' --raw-output --region eu-madrid-1 | base64 -d\r\n\r\nTry it:\r\n  ov stack status\r\n  ov stack logs --tail 50\r\n"]
